From d37227be638ac25bc14973fb88a11b88080caf6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:35:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stop false incidents during normal CCTV activity

Root causes and fixes (details in perception-service/docs/FALSE_POSITIVE_FIXES.md):

- Lingering/intrusion: rules counted buffered "ghost" tracks of people who
  had left, timed dwell from a single first sighting, and reported a
  fabricated confidence (0.5 + dwell/40). Now: active tracks only,
  timestamp-based dwell with exit grace, min inside fraction, per-zone
  dwell/active hours, measured detector confidence, warning for oversized
  placeholder zones.
- Fight: gate paired ghost/duplicate tracks and opened on box jitter; an
  incident came from the clip score alone. Now: active distinct tracks,
  smoothed speed, and a track-level interaction check (close for >= 1 s,
  agitated motion) before any fight incident.
- Fire/smoke: static look-alikes passed frame persistence and the learned
  verifier never forgot old approvals. Now: in-box flicker/growth vs scene
  check, verifier reset per episode, mean (not peak) confidence.
- Unusual activity: threshold from training footage fired on this camera's
  normal motion. Now: per-camera calibration (p99 of 5 min normal) saved
  per checkpoint; honest anomaly score.
- Reports carry confidence_basis and validation_version; read-only audit
  scripts for the dashboard DB and incidents.jsonl (no deletions).
- test_false_positives.py: 26 normal-vs-genuine scenarios.

No model weights changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018GjLCeJAMZch8Mz5HnJkiK
